================================================================================
=== REASONING ===
================================================================================

ADR-015 compliance is preserved by these structural choices:

1. **I1 default-off + I7 per-feature opt-in**: the registry entry's
   `DefaultOn: false` plus the existing `ai.GuardedHandler` middleware
   chain (mode-and-toggle gate from F0 + F6) guarantees the route 404s
   in off mode and remains hidden when the per-feature flag is false.

2. **I3 baseline intact**: BatteryDegradationHandler.Predict and
   BatteryDegradationHandler.Health remain the canonical sources of the
   deterministic forecast. The AI handler invokes the SAME pipeline
   (synthesizeBatterySnapshots → predictDegradation → computeRiskFactors
   + the SAME charging_sessions SELECT) via a production adapter that
   composes existing pkg-level helpers. The chart, hero cards, insights
   and recommendations on BatteryHealthPage are entirely untouched
   apart from a new <FadeIn> AI section inserted ABOVE the hero (so
   even if the AI section renders blank the canonical content below
   continues to flow).

3. **I4 zero egress** in off mode: the strategy is never registered with
   any provider when `ai_mode='off'` because the F1 provider port is
   short-circuited by F0 before strategy dispatch; the new route is
   wrapped with `ai.GuardedHandler('battery-health-forecast-narrative')`
   which returns 404 before reaching the handler body.

4. **I5 hidden UI**: `withAiFeature('battery-health-forecast-narrative',
   InnerSection)` wraps the new React surface. The HOC reads
   `useAiEnabled()` which short-circuits on `ai_mode='off'` OR
   `ai_features['battery-health-forecast-narrative'] !== true`. The
   off-mode contract test mounts the component with both extremes
   (mode='off' + toggle=true, and mode='cloud' + toggle=false) AND a
   positive control (mode='cloud' + toggle=true) to prove the gate
   actually fires.

5. **I6 404 routes**: the new POST /api/v1/ai/battery/health/narrate
   route is mounted through `mountAIRoutes` with the standard
   `ai.GuardedHandler`. The off-mode handler test
   `TestBatteryHealthNarrativeAIOffShowsChartOnly_RouteIs404` proves
   the guard short-circuits to 404 before the inner handler runs
   (the inner is wired to a poison-pill 500 to make the gate's
   short-circuit unambiguous).

6. **I10 type system**: the feature ID
   `battery-health-forecast-narrative` is registered exactly once in
   `internal/ai/features/registry.go` and mirrored into
   `web/src/ai/features.ts` by `tools/aigen`. `tools/aivet` confirms
   the registry route metadata matches the actually-mounted routes
   in `internal/api/ai_routes.go` (RouteSet.Backend matches +
   RouteSet.Frontend matches + RouteSet.UITestIDs match the wrapped
   component's data-testid).

7. **I12 client/bg**: no service worker chunks, no background jobs, no
   push kinds, no client storage keys are introduced by this slice.
   The Off-mode contract impact section in the prompt lists `JobNames:
   []string{}` and `PushKinds: []string{}` explicitly; the registry
   entry uses explicit empty `[]string{}` literals (not omitted) so
   `features.CoverageOK()` sees them as intentionally empty.

**Tool surface area chosen for read-only narration**:
The slice prompt allows tool `query_battery_health_forecast` only.
The tool returns a typed envelope that mirrors the deterministic
forecast (capacity_wh, soh_pct, degradation_pct, slope, projected
soh@5y, dominant charging habits, ranked risk factors). The
production adapter reuses the SAME helpers as the canonical
handler — `lookupVehicleCapacityWh`, `synthesizeBatterySnapshots`,
`(&BatteryDegradationHandler{}).predictDegradation` (the receiver
fields are unused, verified by reading the method body), the SAME
charging_sessions SELECT, and `computeRiskFactors`. This guarantees
the narrator never sees a different forecast from the chart.

**NeedsRAG=false** is deliberate. The forecast is a numeric envelope
grounded in TimescaleDB aggregates; free-text retrieval would
introduce noise and tempt the model to ground in unrelated docs. The
strategy's SystemPrompt explicitly instructs the model to ground
every sentence in the typed envelope and refuse if asked about
another vehicle.

**Redaction policy** `PolicyBatteryHealthForecastNarrative` allows
`ClassVehicleName` only (ModeRedactedTags) — battery metrics are
aggregate numbers, not PII, but the vehicle name is needed for the
narration to feel grounded. Lat/long, addresses, place names, and
charging-location identifiers remain tagged.

